course: dictionary
lesson: 11025
title: A word that is not English
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from other alphabets. You cannot always find them in an English dictionary, but the words around them can tell you what they are doing. Read the whole line first and look for clues.
explain: «The letter waw» tells you waw is a letter, not a word you would use in a sentence about your day. «Psalm 119: Waw» tells you it is a heading. In a Bible, the heading shows which part of the poem comes next.
explain: The Hebrew letters go in order, like A, B, C in English: Aleph, Beth, Gimel, and so on, up to Waw. Waw comes sixth. When you see a name like this, check whether it is a letter, a sound or a label before you guess its meaning.
fact: Waw is the sixth letter of the Hebrew alphabet.
fact: In Hebrew, waw can sound like "v", or stand for an "o" or "u" sound.
fact: Waw is also the name of the Arabic letter و, which sounds like "w" or a long "oo".
fact: In some Bibles, Psalm 119 has 22 parts, each headed by a Hebrew letter, and the sixth part is headed «Waw» or «Vau».
fact: Waw is not an English word. Online, «waw» is sometimes a misspelling of «wow».
exercise: Waw is the sixth letter of which alphabet? | Greek | English | Latin | *Hebrew
exercise: In «Psalm 119: Waw», what is Waw? | *A heading for one section of a long poem | A bird that lives in the desert | The name of a church
exercise: Is waw an English word? | Yes, it means a kind of hat | *No, it is not an English word | Yes, it means a bird | Yes, it means wow
test: The Arabic letter و is called waw. Which English sound does it make? | sh | *w, or a long oo | th | k
test: Online, «waw» sometimes appears as a misspelling of which word? | Hello | *Wow | Walk | Water
exam: In Hebrew, waw can sound like which English letter? | *v | z | k | m
